-- Still true from earlier versions: no library, no http fetches, every
-- element hand-built, per-property pcall in mk(), the whole build inside
-- one pcall'd task.spawn closure, watchdog re-parents if flushed.
-- v3.3.7 (user: "for cmdlist and cmdbar it only creates the screengui
-- for reason, make it create all of them"): POPULATE-THEN-PARENT -- both
-- ScreenGuis are built OUT while still unparented and only enter the
-- KAHX_UI folder once fully populated (a blocked write into a
-- CoreGui-resident gui can no longer leave empty shells), mk() parents
-- through pcall, a verification step fails the load with the exact
-- "ui did not be created" message when a core element is missing, and
-- the watchdog re-homes screens the executor flushed EMPTY.
